The design I'm going with:

- **Converter (tool side):** a debounced watch session. Each pass compares a content snapshot of the project against the last one and only runs a cook when it changed. The cook itself is incremental through the existing cache, and output-dir events are ignored. That makes the snapshot comparison the loop guard. OS backends are inotify on Linux and ReadDirectoryChangesW on Windows.
- **Runtime (engine/assets):** `AssetHandle::reload()` loads the new file on a job and stages the result. `commit_reload()` swaps it in at a safe point. A failed reload keeps the old payload and records the error.

